WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.680
<b>Miyazumi Tatsuru 
Shiratori Mikoto</b>

00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:04.730
Good effort.

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:08.780
<i>I won't let it fall!</i>

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:17.180
Mikoto!

00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:26.380
Any pain?

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:28.730
I'm fine.

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:32.290
Fortunately, you didn't hit your eyeball.

00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:35.370
However, it could be dangerous 
if the wound opens any wider.

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:39.440
To be on the safe side, you should 
have it checked out at a hospital.

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:41.480
Understood. We'll reach 
out to one right away—

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:43.100
I'd like some painkillers, please.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:46.060
What are you talking about? 
You're going to the hospital <i>now</i>.

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:47.520
I'll go after we've won.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:49.410
Don't be stupid.

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:52.550
Shiratori, you shouldn't 
underestimate an eye injury.

00:00:52.930 --> 00:00:56.560
It could end your badminton career.

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:58.820
I'm all right. I can play.

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:01.290
All right? Are you insane?

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:04.750
Please. I want to play.

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:13.670
<b>Miyazumi Tatsuru 
Shiratori Mikoto</b>

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:13.670
<b>Kirishima Takuma 
Izumo Naohiro</b>

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:15.560
Do you think Shiratori-kun's all right?

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:17.950
<b><i>#12 Skyrocket</i></b>

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:19.600
Even if he's able to return 
to play, it won't be easy.

00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:30.110
What, you're gonna keep playing?

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:32.780
Fortunately, he didn't hit the eye itself.

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:35.530
We'll take him to the hospital 
to get it checked after this.

00:01:35.530 --> 00:01:37.410
But in his current condition...

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:40.990
If I think he's in danger, I'll pull
him out, even if it's match point.

00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:44.250
Love all, begin!

00:01:47.890 --> 00:01:50.080
<i>I need to cover for him.</i>

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:56.530
It's all he can do to return their shots.

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:07.690
Hey, Mikoto...

00:02:08.490 --> 00:02:11.940
Could you buy us a little more time?

00:02:12.910 --> 00:02:15.200
I'll figure something out in the meantime.

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:15.990
But...

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:17.740
Please.

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:21.700
Fine.

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:27.210
<i>If we lose this game, 
my badminton career's over.</i>

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:31.250
<i>But if we keep this up, Mikoto will...</i>

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:35.000
<i>We have to hurry.</i>

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:37.140
<i>We need to get Mikoto 
to the hospital, fast.</i>

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:41.180
Damn it!

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:43.730
What the heck am I doing?

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:45.400
No, that was my fault.

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:47.350
This is ridiculous.

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:51.190
Do you just want everyone to know 
you'll keep fighting despite your injury?

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:53.860
Are you that desperate for sympathy?

00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:57.500
Luck's not on your side either, old man.

00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:00.130
Not only have you been 
saddled with this loser,

00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:04.960
but now you have to look after him 
while he just sits around on the court.

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:08.200
You should seriously consider 
breaking up your team.

00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:13.340
It seems like no one's told you 
this before, so I'll tell you.

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:14.170
Huh?

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:19.260
Don't mock someone who's 
trying their best, shithead.

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:20.660
What?

00:03:47.270 --> 00:03:48.950
<i>He's so focused.</i>

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:52.410
<i>Kirishima's taunts backfired.</i>

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:54.530
Tatsu-san's amazing!

00:03:54.530 --> 00:03:56.150
He clearly sees where the shuttle's going.

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:05.800
Miyazumi-san's movements have changed 
completely since the other day.

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:07.340
It's his core.

00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:08.930
What does that mean?

00:04:09.170 --> 00:04:10.130
Yukei.

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:15.670
I see. By strengthening his core, he's 
vastly improved his stability and control.

00:04:15.670 --> 00:04:16.570
Right, Tetsu-san?

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:20.070
It's always muscles that 
matter the most in the end!

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:21.280
You guys are actually right.

00:04:24.310 --> 00:04:28.530
<i>His years of experience and hard work 
have blossomed in this crucial match.</i>

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:33.000
<i>You've shown everyone here the underlying 
strength of a veteran, Tatsu.</i>

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:36.840
<i>Don't get ahead of yourselves!</i>

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:44.930
<i>It won't be that easy, huh?</i>

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:56.140
Crap, they've got us on the defensive!

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:02.150
<i>A drop!</i>

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:06.070
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:18.460
<b>Miyazumi Tatsuru
 Shiratori Mikoto</b>

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:18.460
<b>Kirishima Takuma 
Izumo Naohiro</b>

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:23.290
Thanks for waiting.

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:25.810
What about your eye?

00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:29.680
It's fine now. Anyway, 
let's do you-know-what.

00:05:29.980 --> 00:05:30.900
Sure.

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:36.230
Man, I can't keep up with you.

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:42.360
Is he okay?

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:51.680
<i>There it is.</i>

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:53.160
<i>That's Izumo's habit.</i>

00:05:54.150 --> 00:05:56.960
<i>He adjusts his grip position 
by the slightest amount.</i>

00:05:56.960 --> 00:05:58.830
<i>It signals that he's about 
to hit a hairpin shot.</i>

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:03.130
<b>Miyazumi Tatsuru
 Shiratori Mikoto</b>

00:06:01.310 --> 00:06:03.130
<b>Kirishima Takuma 
Izumo Naohiro</b>

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:07.800
<i>He changed it again.</i>

00:06:10.610 --> 00:06:12.050
<i>They're predicting my shots?</i>

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:18.730
Second game won by Sunlight Beverage.

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:20.930
All right!

00:06:20.010 --> 00:06:20.930
Yes!

00:06:20.930 --> 00:06:22.440
They tied it up.

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:31.570
Operation Rice Ball actually worked.

00:06:31.570 --> 00:06:34.510
I absolutely refuse to call it that.

00:06:34.510 --> 00:06:35.330
Aw, man.

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:38.110
You know,

00:06:38.810 --> 00:06:41.040
playing with you is fun after all.

00:06:45.390 --> 00:06:47.510
You're telling me that now?

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:55.570
Hey.

00:06:57.080 --> 00:06:58.980
I don't need you anymore.

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:02.140
Love all, begin!

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:06.710
<i>I can win this by myself.</i>

00:07:10.640 --> 00:07:14.410
<i>Since I was a kid, I've 
been good at all sports.</i>

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:17.020
Are you really a beginner?

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:19.830
That spike was so fast.

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:23.750
<i>But that doesn't mean I took things easy.</i>

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:28.630
Takuma's a regular already. 
Must be nice being that talented.

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:32.720
His parents are athletes. 
He's made from different stuff.

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:39.060
<i>No matter how hard I worked, people 
would call it "talent" or "natural ability."</i>

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:41.770
<i>It made me angry.</i>

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:47.610
<i>People called my brother a 
prodigy from a young age, too.</i>

00:07:51.060 --> 00:07:57.100
<i>So he was the only one who 
understood how I felt.</i>

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:05.580
<b>12th National Elementary School 
Badminton Tournament 
Welcome 
Open 12/23 (Fri) ~ 12/27 (Tues)</b>

00:08:09.230 --> 00:08:12.220
You won. What's with the doom and gloom?

00:08:12.830 --> 00:08:17.440
People said it's because our parents are 
top athletes, or that I'm a prodigy again.

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:23.320
Let 'em talk. I know you 
didn't win by taking it easy.

00:08:23.320 --> 00:08:24.940
Isn't that enough?

00:08:25.370 --> 00:08:30.030
I'm going to join a corporate 
team and become your partner.

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:33.490
Sure thing! In that case, 
you'll have to get even stronger.

00:08:34.040 --> 00:08:35.680
Quit it!

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:41.040
I missed again.

00:08:41.280 --> 00:08:43.710
You'll need more practice 
before you can beat me.

00:08:43.710 --> 00:08:45.410
Damn it.

00:08:51.530 --> 00:08:53.340
Come on, Bro.

00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:55.450
You held back, didn't you?

00:08:57.330 --> 00:09:01.680
<i>After that day, my brother 
stopped playing against me.</i>

00:09:02.630 --> 00:09:04.950
Is it because I'm not good enough?

00:09:06.720 --> 00:09:09.690
Are you really moving out?

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:13.030
Yeah. I want to focus on badminton.

00:09:21.310 --> 00:09:22.500
Liar.

00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:29.670
<i>Until now, I've played with and 
against all kinds of players.</i>

00:09:30.420 --> 00:09:34.610
<i>But none of them were strong like my brother.</i>

00:09:35.090 --> 00:09:37.050
<i>Not that it matters.</i>

00:09:37.590 --> 00:09:40.010
<i>They're all just stepping stones</i>

00:09:40.540 --> 00:09:43.060
<i>for me to become stronger.</i>

00:09:51.170 --> 00:09:55.320
<i>Partnership? That's something 
the weak talk about.</i>

00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:59.660
<i>I've always fought and won alone.</i>

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:05.640
He really is the world's 
number-one ranked player.

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:15.260
<i>Why isn't he moving?</i>

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:21.180
<i>I don't know what happened, 
but if only Kirishima's attacking...</i>

00:10:28.900 --> 00:10:31.480
<i>Are they predicting Kirishima's moves, too?</i>

00:10:32.110 --> 00:10:34.200
Yes! His foresight is working!

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:36.570
Wait, doesn't it seem like 
Tatsuru-san's doing it, too?

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:39.530
It's working.

00:10:41.180 --> 00:10:45.660
Kirishima Takuma aims wherever's 
least convenient for his opponents.

00:10:46.020 --> 00:10:50.210
I believe we can use that 
to predict his shots.

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:54.170
So we'll use his super unpleasant 
personality against him.

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:56.000
<b></b>72nd National Japanese Corporate Tournament

00:10:54.550 --> 00:10:59.690
Anyway, we're going to watch all 
his previous matches and study him.

00:10:59.690 --> 00:11:00.970
Ugh...

00:11:05.810 --> 00:11:06.410
Kirishima.

00:11:06.410 --> 00:11:07.450
Shut up.

00:11:17.330 --> 00:11:20.650
<i>Until now, I've always chosen the best path.</i>

00:11:21.580 --> 00:11:23.250
<i>I transferred to Mitsuhoshi</i>

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:26.740
<i>and teamed up with Kirishima,
 the world's number-one ranked player.</i>

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:30.040
<i>Every choice I made was 
meant to take me higher.</i>

00:11:30.680 --> 00:11:34.460
<i>Right now it's better for me to 
stand still than to upset Kirishima.</i>

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:36.670
<i>That's the best choice.</i>

00:11:37.610 --> 00:11:39.170
Damn it.

00:11:39.630 --> 00:11:40.520
Sorry.

00:11:40.520 --> 00:11:42.130
We'll get the next one.

00:11:42.850 --> 00:11:43.680
Sorry.

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:45.140
Focus on the next point.

00:11:53.700 --> 00:11:55.230
Ridiculous.

00:11:58.130 --> 00:11:59.260
<i>Damn it.</i>

00:12:03.530 --> 00:12:06.660
<i>This isn't doubles!</i>

00:12:09.530 --> 00:12:11.660
What do you think you're doing?

00:12:11.660 --> 00:12:14.050
Kirishima, stop attacking.

00:12:14.050 --> 00:12:14.880
What?

00:12:15.520 --> 00:12:17.670
They're predicting your attacks.

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:20.420
If you keep attacking recklessly, 
you'll just burn your stamina.

00:12:21.020 --> 00:12:23.130
Are you trying to say I'll lose?

00:12:23.130 --> 00:12:26.680
No, I'm saying we should change our strategy.

00:12:26.940 --> 00:12:29.970
We'll use their own strategy against them.

00:12:30.540 --> 00:12:34.740
We'll start playing defensively 
and let them attack.

00:12:35.220 --> 00:12:38.770
They're exhausted. They'll create an opening.

00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:41.530
We'll strike then. How does that sound?

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:50.330
<i>A clear?</i>

00:12:55.980 --> 00:12:59.770
<i>Looks like we're playing a real match now.</i>

00:13:12.150 --> 00:13:14.850
It's Mitsuhoshi's match point.

00:13:25.090 --> 00:13:26.910
They're safe from match point!

00:13:58.260 --> 00:14:01.420
Mikoto, we've played enough.

00:14:02.720 --> 00:14:03.900
No.

00:14:04.450 --> 00:14:07.550
Your badminton career will continue.

00:14:07.550 --> 00:14:09.940
This isn't the only match you'll play.

00:14:09.940 --> 00:14:10.950
You know that, don't you?

00:14:12.700 --> 00:14:16.050
But if we lose this match, then you...

00:14:16.050 --> 00:14:17.540
And you're okay with that?!

00:14:19.100 --> 00:14:20.990
I've played enough.

00:14:21.500 --> 00:14:25.150
I made it this far with you 
and the rest of the team.

00:14:25.600 --> 00:14:26.910
That's enough for me.

00:14:27.480 --> 00:14:28.970
What are you talking about?

00:14:30.120 --> 00:14:32.370
I love the way you play.

00:14:32.370 --> 00:14:33.870
I want to watch you play forever.

00:14:35.200 --> 00:14:38.180
I want you to keep playing.

00:14:38.180 --> 00:14:40.920
So let's forfeit the match.

00:14:47.610 --> 00:14:49.110
What do you mean, you want to watch?!

00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:51.560
I...

00:14:53.390 --> 00:14:55.290
My badminton...

00:14:55.290 --> 00:14:57.870
It means nothing without you by my side!

00:15:03.330 --> 00:15:06.590
Badaryman, keep it up!

00:15:06.590 --> 00:15:10.720
Badaryman, you can do it!

00:15:11.180 --> 00:15:14.830
You can do it!

00:15:19.060 --> 00:15:21.750
Everybody make some noise!

00:15:22.130 --> 00:15:23.890
Go, go, let's go!

00:15:23.890 --> 00:15:25.480
Go, go, SunBev!

00:15:25.710 --> 00:15:27.410
Go, go, let's go!

00:15:27.410 --> 00:15:28.690
Go, go, SunBev!

00:15:29.090 --> 00:15:30.570
Go, go, let's go!

00:15:30.570 --> 00:15:32.450
Go, go, SunBev!

00:15:32.450 --> 00:15:34.030
Go, go, let's go!

00:15:34.030 --> 00:15:35.770
Go, go, SunBev!

00:15:34.350 --> 00:15:36.160
Wow...

00:15:35.770 --> 00:15:37.390
Go, go, let's go!

00:15:37.390 --> 00:15:39.090
Go, go, SunBev!

00:15:39.090 --> 00:15:40.620
Go, go, let's go!

00:15:40.620 --> 00:15:42.400
Go, go, SunBev!

00:15:41.730 --> 00:15:44.830
Hey, Mikoto. Do you mind 
if I get a little greedy?

00:15:42.400 --> 00:15:44.220
Go, go, let's go!

00:15:44.220 --> 00:15:45.850
Go, go, SunBev!

00:15:45.850 --> 00:15:47.560
Go, go, let's go!

00:15:46.200 --> 00:15:49.180
I want to win this match.

00:15:47.560 --> 00:15:49.180
Go, go, SunBev!

00:15:49.180 --> 00:15:53.420
I don't want to let anyone 
else stand at your side.

00:15:49.190 --> 00:15:50.780
Go, go, let's go!

00:15:50.780 --> 00:15:52.540
Go, go, SunBev!

00:15:55.470 --> 00:15:58.300
You're telling me that <i>now</i>?

00:16:05.270 --> 00:16:07.480
<b>Miyazumi</b>

00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:11.610
<i>You can't be serious.</i>

00:16:13.590 --> 00:16:15.870
<i>I'm going to win!</i>

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:19.870
<i>I'll do my best.</i>

00:16:21.100 --> 00:16:22.970
<i>In our current state...</i>

00:16:24.680 --> 00:16:25.670
<i>We can win!</i>

00:16:27.460 --> 00:16:30.670
<b>Miyazumi Tatsuru 
Shiratori Mikoto</b>

00:16:27.460 --> 00:16:30.670
<b>Kirishima Takuma
 Izumo Naohiro</b>

00:16:29.250 --> 00:16:30.670
It's match point.

00:16:30.670 --> 00:16:33.090
One more point!

00:16:33.370 --> 00:16:35.010
I'll handle the back.

00:16:36.710 --> 00:16:39.100
<i>Yeah, I'm fine. I'll handle the back.</i>

00:16:53.190 --> 00:16:54.570
Tatsuru!

00:17:09.590 --> 00:17:16.590
Game and match won by Miyazumi Tatsuru and 
Shiratori Mikoto of Sunlight Beverage!

00:17:10.770 --> 00:17:14.380
<b>Miyazumi Tatsuru 
Shiratori Mikoto</b>

00:17:10.770 --> 00:17:14.380
<b>Kirishima Takuma 
Izumo Naohiro 
</b>Mitsuhoshi Bank

00:17:18.600 --> 00:17:20.280
Yeah!

00:17:23.510 --> 00:17:25.560
Wow!

00:17:25.560 --> 00:17:27.520
Thanks!

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:29.230
All right!

00:17:29.230 --> 00:17:30.940
Wow!

00:17:32.650 --> 00:17:34.360
Nice game!

00:17:36.930 --> 00:17:38.490
We're holding a meeting when we get back.

00:17:46.470 --> 00:17:48.880
Go cool your heads for a while.

00:17:48.880 --> 00:17:50.050
Yes, sir.

00:17:59.300 --> 00:18:00.880
Why the long face?

00:18:03.620 --> 00:18:04.770
Bro.

00:18:06.400 --> 00:18:11.690
Next time, let's face 
each other in the finals.

00:18:13.700 --> 00:18:17.680
Also, Mom says to stop by the house sometime.

00:18:18.910 --> 00:18:20.850
She sent me a message, too.

00:18:20.850 --> 00:18:24.370
We should probably visit once in a 
while to eat Mom's Hamburg steaks.

00:18:24.990 --> 00:18:26.500
You love those, don't you?

00:18:27.200 --> 00:18:28.980
Do you even know how long ago that was?

00:18:31.910 --> 00:18:34.840
I lost the bet.

00:18:35.610 --> 00:18:40.820
I know you care about the company 
more than anything else.

00:18:42.380 --> 00:18:47.570
It's true that corporate sports 
don't produce any direct benefit.

00:18:47.570 --> 00:18:49.520
They come with costs, too.

00:18:50.100 --> 00:18:51.260
But...

00:18:52.250 --> 00:18:55.110
Thank you for your support!

00:18:55.490 --> 00:18:57.570
Thank you!

00:18:59.310 --> 00:19:02.420
This excitement isn't meaningless.

00:19:02.420 --> 00:19:07.000
Their efforts bring together 
the hearts of many.

00:19:07.860 --> 00:19:13.590
It may be invisible, but
 I believe it's indispensable.

00:19:24.590 --> 00:19:26.160
That's good.

00:19:26.970 --> 00:19:27.540
Crap.

00:19:27.540 --> 00:19:29.580
What? Is it your knee?

00:19:30.320 --> 00:19:31.980
The elastic on my underwear broke.

00:19:52.510 --> 00:19:54.810
Hello, thank you for your continued—

00:19:54.810 --> 00:19:57.250
